Z||000000||Linx||10-26-1999||06:58 PM||||Fello Fiero Knucklebusters-<P>During the ceremonial replacement of the intake manifold gaskets, I discovered these injectors...there are two different kinds on my fuel rail.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/linxramblr/injecto2.jpg">   <P>Anyone seen these flat tipped ones before?  Heck- shouldnt they all be the same kind?<P>Four of 'em are the same...they can be best described as having hats     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  -little plastic covers over the orifice.   One of them was missing the "hat".<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/linxramblr/injector.jpg">   <P>I have to replace the whole injector for a missing plastic "hat"?  And what about the two odd injectors; with the flat tips?  Are they standard?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 10-26-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||10-26-1999||07:40 PM||||When I pulled my engine apart one of my injectors was missing a "hat" too.  I think it was so old it broke up on itself.  Just to see what I could see, I asked the guy at Advanced Auto Parts if he sold replacement hats.  He did!  The pack of injector odds and ends included all the O-rings and little washers to remount your injectors.  I think the injectors themselves are fine, so I'll just replace the consumables.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||10-27-1999||03:41 PM||||Grrrrrrr.  I went to Autozone, and all they had in the way of seal kits was a bag of o-rings.  No hats.  The injectors they had in stock were of the flat tipped variety, and go for a whoppin' $50 each.<P>Advance had the same inj. at $31. Go figure.  <I>But no hats.</I>  I cant beleive that this lack-of-hat is gonna hold up my reassembly.<P>Any chance you still have the part number on the seals you got from Advance?<P><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 10-27-1999).]||||reg||1
